  "dct_description_sm": [
    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us6000syc2](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us6000syc2) Magnitude 5.7 earthquake at 56.032 depth occurred on May 17 2026 86 km ENE of Severo-Kuril’sk, Russia. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude 50.8432 longitude 157.3229. It impacted 25 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
